1
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:08,000
Deng baş temaşevanên me yên hêja, temaşevanên me yên ezîz,
ez bi hêvî me hûn gişt nav xêr û xweşiyê da bin.
 
Hello to our precious viewers, our dear viewers, I hope you
are all well and happy.

2
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Ez hatim bi vîdyoyekî xwaş û vîdyoyekî ecêb.
 
I have come with a nice and wonderful video.

3
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:14,000
Vîdyoya me her wekî hûn dibînin li deştî cîrê me ye, bi
rastî dîtineke dîmenekî zeytûnan e.
 
Our video, as you can see, is in the plains, truly it is a
beautiful view of the olives.

4
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:17,000
Em kêfa me heye em vîdyoyekê nav zeytûnan de derbas bikin.
 
We are delighted to spend a video among the olives.

5
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
Û kî ji me re nivîsî bûn kî daxwazên em derbas bikin an em
vîdyoyan çêkin, hûn dikarin binivîsin.
 
And whoever writes to us, whatever requests you want us to
do or make videos, you can write.

6
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Wekî çawa xwedanên me sibehê radibin tên nav zeytûnan, em jî
rabin werin vîdyoyan ji we re çêkin.
 
Just as our people wake up in the morning and come to the
olives, we also wake up and come to make videos for you.

7
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:27,000
Em kêfa me heye gî nav zeytûnan de derbas bikin.
 
We are delighted to spend it all among the olives.

8
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:33,000
Bi rastî em ê derbasî cem kekê Dilbirîn bin, kekê Dilbirîn
jî çîrokeke gelekî pir xweş pêşkêşî me kiriye.
 
Actually, we will go to brother Dilbirîn, brother Dilbirîn
has presented a very beautiful story for us.

9
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:38,000
Piştî bîst û şeş salan ji Brîtanyayê vegeriyaye, hatiye
Badîna û gundê me,
 
After 26 years he returned from Britain, came to Badîna and
our village,

10
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:42,000
û hatiye nav milk û malê xwe. Lê dayîka gundî jî, wê jî da
xuyakirin,
 
and came to his own property and home. But a village mother
is also here, she also showed,

11
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:48,000
dayika me, em kanin bêjin vegeriyaye. Ew jî piştî deh û sê
salan, ew jî vegeriyaye Badîna û hatiye nav milk û malê xwe.
 
our mother, we can say she has returned. She also returned
to Badîna after 13 years and came to her property and home.

12
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Di têştê da vîdyoyê da xweş, dayîkê ji me re klorikek Badîno
çêkiriye,
 
In the breakfast of this video, the mother has prepared a
Badîna flatbread for us,

13
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
yanî em ê bên, em ê rojeke Efrînî bext û bextiyar derbas
bikin.
 
which means we will come and spend a happy and lucky Afrin
day.

14
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:59,000
Bi me re bin, û bi me re bimînin, em vîdyoyekê xweş û kibar
bi hevre derbas bikin.
 
Be with us, and stay with us, so we can spend a nice and
polite video together.

15
00:01:59,000 --> 00:02:04,000
Berî em dest bi vîdyoya xwe bikin, bîr nekin qenala Hatim Li
Efrînê piştgirî bikin,
 
Before we start our video, do not forget to support the
"Hatim Li Efrînê" channel,

16
00:02:04,000 --> 00:02:08,000
û kî jî ji me re şîroveyan bike çi daxwazên em derbas bikin,
yan li benda kîjan pirsan bin, ji me re şîroveyan çêbikin.
 
and whoever comments for us, what requests you want us to
fulfill, or whatever questions you have, make comments for
us.

17
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:22,000
De bi me re bin, bi hevre em kerem bikin cem kekê Dilbirîn.
 
So be with us, let's go together to brother Dilbirîn.

18
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:27,000
Belê temaşevanên me yên hêja, bi rastî ez pir kêfxweş im bi
dîtina kekê me Dilbirîn, û dayîka Dilo.
 
Yes, our dear viewers, truly I am very happy to see our
brother Dilbirîn, and mother Dilo.

19
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:32,000
Kekê Dilbirîn piştî bîst û şeş salan hat Badîna û hat nav
milk û malê xwe.
 
Brother Dilbirîn returned to Badîna and came to his property
and home after 26 years.

20
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:34,000
Dayê piştî deh û sê salan ew jî vegeriya.
 
Mother also returned after 13 years.

21
00:02:34,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Lê em ê bi hevre kekê Dilbirîn ji nêzîk ve nas bikin û dayê.
 
But we will get to know brother Dilbirîn and mother closely
together.

22
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Merheba ji we re.
 
Hello to you.

23
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Ehlen wa sehlen, kekê Xelîl, ser çava.
 
You are welcome, brother Xelîl, upon my eyes (you are very
welcome).

24
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:41,000
Tu çawa yî dayê?
 
How are you, mother?

25
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:42,000
Hemdullah sax bî.
 
Thank God, may you be healthy.

26
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Welleh ez pir kêfxweş im bi dîtina we.
 
By God, I am very happy to see you.

27
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Welleh ez ji te pirtir kêf-, kêftir im, û xwaştir me.
 
By God, I am even happier than you, and more pleased.

28
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:50,000
Li an ku ev hatin û welatê xwe dîtin.
 
Because they came and saw their country.

29
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:53,000
Ê gişt em Heleb, seqî dinya giştik bûye bi me.
 
We were all in Aleppo, the whole world became a foreign
place to us.

30
00:02:53,000 --> 00:02:55,000
Û piştî ev hatin, hîn em hatin Efrîn...
 
And after they came, when we came to Afrin...

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Hîn nefesê we fireh bû.
 
Your breath became wider (you felt relieved).

32
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

33
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Bi rastî ez pir kêfxweş im, dayê.
 
Truly I am very happy, mother.

34
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:03,000
Sax bî...
 
May you be healthy...

35
00:03:03,000 --> 00:03:06,000
Qenatî me, qenatî Hatim li Efrînê... Kekê Dilo, her kesek we
li Efrînê ha bikî wara...
 
Our channel, the Hatim Li Efrînê channel... Brother Dilo,
whoever of you works in Afrin...

36
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Ehlen wa sehlen ser çava, hezar car ser çava... xêr hatin.
 
You are welcome, a thousand times welcome... welcome.

37
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Tu bixêr hatî kekê Dilo.
 
Welcome, brother Dilo.

38
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:11,000
Sax bî xweş bî, sipas kek Xelîl.
 
May you be healthy and happy, thanks brother Xelîl.

39
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Ez daxwazim, ka hûn kanin ji me re xeberek din, em dê kerî
dest pê bikin, tu ji kî derê derketî, çûkî kî derê, tu ketî
kî derê, tu çûkî kî derê ji Badîna...
 
I request, could you tell us a bit about how you started,
where you left from, where you went, where you ended up,
where did you go from Badîna...

40
00:03:19,000 --> 00:03:22,000
Bi xwedê, kekê Xelîl, min pir dît milet, û ez pir geriyam...
 
By God, brother Xelîl, I saw many people, and I traveled a
lot...

41
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Silav... bi temamî... ez çûme Yûnanê, sal û nîvekê min li
Yûnanê mabûm.
 
Completely... I went to Greece, I stayed in Greece for a
year and a half.

42
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Teqriben ev e... paşê jî sala... sala hezar û...
 
Approximately that is it... then the year... the year
nineteen hundred and...

43
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
neh sed û nod û çara... ez çûme Swêd.
 
nineteen hundred and ninety-four... I went to Sweden.

44
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Erê, heta sala dused û bîst... hezar û...
 
Yes, until the year two thousand and...

45
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Teqrîben bîst û yek sal ez li Swêd mam.
 
I stayed in Sweden for approximately 21 years.

46
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:37,000
Û noka jî, pênc, şeş sal ez li Brîtanya me.
 
Yes.

47
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:41,000
Û noka jî, pênc, şeş sal ez li Brîtanya me.
 
And now too, for five or six years I am in Britain.

48
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:48,000
Ê... me dît... xelk, pir me dît, yanî, ji me diqetin... ji
gundan, giştî...
 
Uh... we saw... people, we saw a lot, meaning, we were
completely cut off from the villages...

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Yanî... em gerîn bi teqrîbî.
 
Meaning... we wandered around approximately.

50
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:53,000
Belê. Xweş e xerîbî û çetîn e jî yekî xweş e û nexweş e...
 
Yes. Being abroad is both pleasant and difficult, it is both
good and bad...

51
00:03:53,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Bi xwedê kek Xelîl, xerîbî çetîn e, ne wa meseleyek e.
 
By God, brother Xelîl, being abroad is difficult, it's not a
simple matter.

52
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Tu... heta tu kanî, ev her tişt... wextê ku tu ji Efrîn, ji
minteqeya me derket, te heta çû... ev me dît, yeqîn tu
wendayî...
 
You see... whatever you do... when you left Afrin, from our
region, once you left... we experienced it, believe me you
are lost...

53
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:02,000
Welleh... gişk li benda wê rojê ne ku vegerin.
 
By God... everyone is waiting for the day they return.

54
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

55
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:08,000
Ê dayê te çawa dît tu çûyî, te dît... te zeytûn dît, milk,
mal dît?
 
And mother, how did you see it when you went, you saw... did
you see the olives, the property, the home?

56
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
Malê me ye ro, erqek ji canê me ye ro.
 
It is for our home, it is a vein for our soul.

57
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Nefesa me ye ro.
 
It is our breath.

58
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:20,000
Ê bes ku wa... wey malê me li kî derê, yanî malê we li kî
derê bi îstiqrar bûyî... ew derê xweş e.
 
But the situation is... wherever you are, meaning wherever a
person is settled, that place is nice.

59
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

60
00:04:21,000 --> 00:04:25,000
Erê wira xweş e rinde. Bes hebsa nefes e...
 
Yes, it is nice and good there. But the breathing is
confined.

61
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:26,000
Nefes e me we ra...?
 
We are the breath...?

62
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Erê, tu herî, tu bêyî, yanî te tişt heye... tu... nabe...
 
Yes, you go, you come, meaning you have things... or you
don't.

63
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:36,000
Tu çi bixwazî tu kanî wê deqîqê bikî, yan bikirî. Xwe pê
dîne.
 
Whatever you want, you can make it in a minute, or buy it.
You can occupy yourself with it.

64
00:04:36,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Xwarin pê nîne...
 
There is no lack of food...

65
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:43,000
Ê lê wira, tu dûr xwediyan e, kesekî te lê tune ye.
 
But there, you are far from your people, you have no one
there.

66
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Kes xerîb...
 
Strangers...

67
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:49,000
Erê, hindî hene, pakistanî hene, îraqî hene...
 
Yes, there are Indians, Pakistanis, Iraqis...

68
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Înglîz nîsbet hên nakin.
 
The English themselves are rarely seen.

69
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
Weha de fêde wêre dere.
 
So there is no benefit to it.

70
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:57,000
Kekê Dilo, tu li... tu li Brîtanya dimînî?
 
Brother Dilo, do you live in... do you stay in Britain?

71
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:58,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

72
00:04:58,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Û temaşevanên me yên hêja, ez tiştekî din jî wekî xeber dim,
niha kekê Dilo derbasî ser wê meselê jî ji me re xeber de.
 
And our precious viewers, I will say another thing as well,
now brother Dilo will also talk to us about that matter.

73
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Berî vê demekî min vîdyoyek li ser Yûtûbê daxist, min got
kesê daxwaze tiştekî şehn Ewropa ke, bi riya kekê Dilbirîn,
şîrket şehn li cem heye...
 
A while ago I uploaded a video on YouTube, I said whoever
wants to ship something to Europe, through brother Dilbirîn,
he has a shipping company...

74
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Bi xwedê kekê Xelîl, ev bûn sê sal... teqrîben sê sal hene,
 
By God, brother Xelîl, it's been three years... there are
about three years now.

75
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:25,000
E berê em bi xwe... yanî me tişt tînan û bi xwe jî bi riyekî
xweş tînan. Heleb. Me li Heleb tişt derdikir. Ji tiştên me
ntîqe bî teb'en.
 
Before, we ourselves... meaning we were bringing things, and
we brought them ourselves through a nice route. Aleppo. We
exported things from Aleppo. From our area's things, of
course.

76
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:37,000
Û me tînan Heleb kî teşedekir û çêdikir. Te zanî wextê me ra
dibê Ewropa gerek tu tiştekî... yanî ne wekî tiştên bi derê
çû bî wera firotan malê lazîqî dikir û dikir kartona, mîzamî
dikir...
 
And we brought them to Aleppo, who checked and processed
them. You know, when it comes to Europe, you need a thing...
meaning not like things exported there just for sale, they
made plastic (packaging) for it and put it in cardboard,
organized it...

77
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Ê û ji Heleb me dibrin Lazqiyê û ji Lazqiyê diẍrî dihat...
Brîtanya, London, bê xweş me dibrin mal.
 
So from Aleppo we took it to Latakia, and from Latakia
directly came... to Britain, London, easily we took it home.

78
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
Ê, rawî ser ve fikrê... fikrek hate min.
 
Yes, based on this idea... an idea came to me.

79
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:54,000
Milet pir li cem me li Brîtanya heye... meselen her carekî
ez karim Hollanda, ez derim penêr di Hollanda tînim.
 
We have a lot of people in Britain... for example, every
time I can go to Holland, I go and bring cheese from
Holland.

80
00:05:54,000 --> 00:06:00,000
Bi xwedê malxwe me. Ehbab hene, dost hene, hew dibêjin Dilo
zeytûnê me bîne, hew dibêjin zeytê me bîne, hew dibêjin
nizanim çi bîne...
 
By God, our families. We have loved ones, we have friends,
some say Dilo bring our olives, some say bring our olive
oil, some say bring I don't know what...

81
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Ê paşê fikre hate min.
 
Then the idea came to me.

82
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:04,000
Min got... mesele... xêr e xelkê kî ji Efrîn,
 
I said... for instance... why do people from Afrin,

83
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:08,000
bibin Almanya û tekre ji Almanya... yanî zehmet e. Ji
Brîtanya heta Almaya were pir zehmet e.
 
take it to Germany and then from Germany... meaning it's
difficult. From Britain to Germany it's very difficult.

84
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Min got, çima ez mesele gîyî em dikin. Ko em ê şahnî ke
wekin... yanî nefs nîzamê ke... çi çêke şuxlek garekî dehêşt
em me ra kar e, ceh bike...
 
I said, why don't we do this. Let's do shipping... meaning
the same system... do a job that makes it a business for us,
try...

85
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:15,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

86
00:06:15,000 --> 00:06:31,000
Erê, welleh ev e... di wehşt e, fikir hat min û zatê ti...
eslê bi min ko kekê Xelîl... te ke alîkarî kir me û saetê te
jî xwest alîkarî kirin... yanî bi riya qenatî te, û çendek
din jî alîkarî kirin... yanî seet e giyî xweş e, ez.
 
Yes, by God this is it... it's a good thing, the idea came
to me, and indeed you... basically since you brother
Xelîl... you helped us and those times you also wanted to
help... meaning through your channel, and some others also
helped... meaning it's very nice. I am...

87
00:06:31,000 --> 00:06:35,000
Ez pir kêfxweş im kekê Xelîl. Tiştek din a milletê me de
heye.
 
I am very happy, brother Xelîl. There is another thing in
our people.

88
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Belkî kes mulaxeze nake bes min mulaxeze kirî.
 
Maybe no one notices, but I noticed.

89
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Wextê kî însanek yekî derheqî kî kefî... pir likêlekî gend
diskinin.
 
When a person stands against something... a lot stand beside
you.

90
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:44,000
Belê. Ev tiştek pir xweş e.
 
Yes. This is a very nice thing.

91
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Bes em însan tima hin ... çiqa kelekî ma biskînin ew dibînin
ê wela êkî derê rakî yî ewa kelekî binas kiriye. Ma re temam
xelk nîşan dibe. Wela xelk pir kêlekî biskînin. Şahîdî...
 
But we humans always... no matter how much they stand beside
you, they see it, they say wherever you put it, that one has
stood next to him. To us it shows all the people. By God,
many people will stand beside you. Witnesses...

92
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Noka jî... me şîrket li Mûbatî vekiriye.
 
And now... we have opened a company in Mabeta.

93
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:04,000
Ê, mesela xelkê her li Mûbatî tiştên xwe teslîm ke, û tiştkî
nadin wê derê.
 
So, for example, people will hand over their things in
Mabeta, and they won't pay anything there.

94
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

95
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Em jî ji Mûbatî em ê bibin... Heleb, kî ji nav erdê
derxistin... mesele her yak qedera dika kîjan bajarî.
 
We will also take it from Mabeta... to Aleppo, extract it
from the lands... for example, every piece according to
which city.

96
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:12,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

97
00:07:12,000 --> 00:07:17,000
Û hawî were, ... ê tekin hawî ew ji Lazqiyê diẍrî wera
Brîtanya.
 
And package it, ... make the packages, it goes from Latakia
directly to Britain.

98
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:26,000
Paşê wara cem e mistauda, ez bi takrî wrr girê vêkim. Orde
