û ji kîntiyero...
 
Then it will come to our warehouse, I will independently tie
it up. From there, for example, whichever city it's for, I
will independently take my car and from the container...

99
00:07:26,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Tiştê mûneyê te jî me bala xwe dayê, berî vê vîdyok te ji me
re şand, gî mûneyê destê...
 
We also paid attention to your pantry items, before this you
sent us a video, all pantry items made by the hand of...

100
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:34,000
ê... dayîkê me, dayîkê Efrîn e.
 
our mothers, the mothers of Afrin.

101
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Erê wellah.
 
Yes, by God.

102
00:07:35,000 --> 00:07:44,000
Ji kincîr û gûzan, ji dimsa hinarê, ji zeytûnan, mûneya di
mala giştî cem kekê Dilbirîn heye. Giş kesên li Brîtanya çi
gerek wî bî kane wêrê daxweze.
 
From figs and walnuts, from pomegranate molasses, from
olives, all the house pantry is available with brother
Dilbirîn. Whoever is in Britain, whatever they need, they
can request it there.

103
00:07:44,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Bi xwedê Xelîl, niha mesela... yanî em pir dûr naçin.
 
By God Xelîl, now for example... meaning we don't have to go
too far.

104
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Te reqemeke yekî da min. Bavê Hemûş, li Basûtê.
 
Yes.

105
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Te reqemeke yekî da min. Bavê Hemûş, li Basûtê.
 
You gave me someone's number. Hemûş's father, in Basûtê.

106
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Te got Dilbirîn me pê re têkilî kir, min telefonê lê kir, û
paşê xortan çûn cem gundî, ez ne li vir bûm wê çaxê.
 
You said Dilbirîn we contacted him, I called him, and then
the guys went to the village, I wasn't here at that time.

107
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Ew wê re mesela... giyan kirin... wellah kekê Hemûş jî
seetên xwe xweş xeta nake... wexta dengê xwe dişîne.
 
So there, the issue... they brought it to life... by God
brother Hemûş also has good hours, he doesn't make
mistakes... when he sends his voice.

108
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:11,000
Û înşelleh em ê tim di nav cengê de bin. Em mesela tiştekî
me ji Badîna kirî, noka jî wexta mewsima ye, em hatine,
şênahî ye, xweş e,
 
And hopefully we will always be in the effort. For example
we bought something from Badîna, now it's also the season,
we came, it's green, it's nice,

109
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:16,000
qerebalix e, me jî got em ê mesela zeytûnên xwe bişînin,
pir, yanî, kemiye...
 
it's crowded, we also said we will send our olives, a lot,
meaning, a quantity...

110
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:21,000
û zeytê me jî, ezêkê bikirim, giş çêkim, cahiz bikim, û
înşelleh em ê wê jî bişînin ji milet re.
 
and our oil too, I will buy it, prepare it all, make it
ready, and hopefully we will send that too to the people.

111
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Ê mesela xwedaniyên xwe kî kas li minteqê tune, ew kanibin
cem me bibin,
 
And for example, whoever has no family in the region, they
can get it from us,

112
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
û xwedaniyên xwe jî hene, ê ji gund ra bişînin. Înşelleh em
bi selametî.
 
and those who have family, they will send it from the
village. Hopefully in safety.

113
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:36,000
Û heta ji min tê der, ez ê balim min tiştî xelkê bi selametî
bimale gînê. Heta j'min tê!
 
And as much as I can, I will ensure to deliver people's
things safely to their homes. As much as I can!

114
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Saetên we xweş, bi rastî ez pir kêfxweş bûm, ji miletê me
re, şîrketa şehnê li cem kekê Dilo heye û fira'ekê di li
Mûbata ye.
 
May you have good times, truly I was very happy, for our
people, brother Dilo has a shipping company and a branch in
Mabeta.

115
00:08:46,000 --> 00:08:51,000
Înşelleh, em mûneyên xwe, werin mûneyên me bi şîqek pêve
bin, û em ê bişînin Ewrûpa ji dost û ehbaban re.
 
Hopefully, our pantries, come let's show off our pantries,
and we will send it to Europe to friends and loved ones.

116
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:59,000
Xêrek giran li stuyê we, çi gerek bin dikarin bi kekê
Dilbirîn re deng bikin, em ê nimreya te jî deynin vir, çi
gerek we bin, mûneya malê hûn kanin gişkî ji cem kekê
Dilbirîn bibin.
 
A great blessing on your neck, whatever they need they can
contact brother Dilbirîn, we will put your number here too,
whatever you need, you can get all your house pantry from
brother Dilbirîn.

117
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Kekê Xelîl, lekê tiştekî din jî ra we bibêjim.
 
Brother Xelîl, let me tell you one more thing.

118
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:02,000
Berî vê ez li Brîtanya bûm,
 
Yes.

119
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:04,000
Berî vê ez li Brîtanya bûm,
 
Before this I was in Britain,

120
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Dayîkekê telefonî min kir.
 
A mother called me.

121
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Welleh stirî bi çavê min xistin.
 
Yes.

122
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:08,000
Welleh stirî bi çavê min xistin.
 
By God, they put thorns in my eyes (touched me deeply).

123
00:09:08,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Me çiqas dît dayîkek li ser bida'ê wê de tiştek pirs kir.
 
What did she do? A mother asked something about her goods.

124
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
Go Dilbirîn kekê, wesîyek li te bikim?
 
She said, brother Dilbirîn, may I make a request to you?

125
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Go emanetekî çêkî li ser te be?
 
She said, can you take a trust upon yourself?

126
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
Go, xwedê kekê Dilbirîn ez qurbanê çavê te bim.
 
She said, by God brother Dilbirîn, may I be a sacrifice to
your eyes.

127
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:25,000
Go em li cem xelkê rûdinin, yanî ewa tiştî pir çêbûye bi me
re, wa manî dayikek bi min re wa dipeyive...
 
She said we sit with people, meaning this thing has happened
to us a lot, when a mother talks to me like this...

128
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Go qurbanê li hevrûyê te bim, go bas navê Efrînê xerab
nekin. Pêşeroj î nake Xelîl, stirî bi çavê min ketin.
 
She said, may I be a sacrifice to you, just don't ruin the
name of Afrin. It makes no future Xelîl, tears fell from my
eyes.

129
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:35,000
Welleh yanî ez pir qehirîm. Elhemdulellah carekî ev tişt
nekiriye,
 
By God, meaning I was very saddened. Thank God we have never
done this,

130
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:42,000
Û min xiş nekiriye. Qisûr efû ke, tu xiş şixulî, tu zû
dikevî, bes tu rast şixulî, tu li ser lingê xwe ranê û tu
dewam ke.
 
And I haven't cheated. Forgive the shortcomings, if you work
with cheating, you fall early, but if you work honestly, you
stand on your own feet and you continue.

131
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:44,000
Welleh wê dayîkê pir tesîr kir.
 
By God, that mother had a great effect.

132
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:47,000
Gotineke bav û kalê me heye, têştek şor ew xwariye...
 
There is a saying of our ancestors, he has eaten a salty
dish...

133
00:09:47,000 --> 00:09:48,000
Mhm.
 
Mhm.

134
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:51,000
Bes em kanin em gotinên bav û kalanê...
 
But we can say the words of the ancestors...

135
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:55,000
Ew dizanin tiştê xirab tu jê dûr dikevî.
 
You know, you stay away from the bad things.

136
00:09:55,000 --> 00:10:00,000
[Dikenin]
 
[Laughs]

137
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Lê neyê bîrkirin, gidî daxwaziyeke min ji te heye.
 
But let it not be forgotten, I have a request for you.

138
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:06,000
Gazinekî min heye. Ev çi ji rêça bav û kalên me ye?
 
I have a complaint. What is this from the path of our
ancestors?

139
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:08,000
A re. Serkeftin kekê Dilbîn.
 
Yes. Success, dear Dilbîn.

140
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Saet xweş kek Xelîl, saet xweş.
 
Good hours brother Xelîl, good hours.

141
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Tiştekî te yê xweş ez dibînim, te ev sarme naha berav
kiriye.
 
I see something nice of yours, you've gathered these stuffed
grape leaves (sarme) now.

142
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:15,000
Te tişkî din berav kiriye wisa?
 
Have you gathered anything else like this?

143
00:10:15,000 --> 00:10:19,000
Wileh, xêr û bereketên me, ji nav milkê me ye...
 
By God, our blessings and abundance, are from our land...

144
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:23,000
Xêr û bereketên we, te berav kiriye. Ev sal baraneke baş
barî, xêr û bereket hebû.
 
Your blessings and abundance, you have gathered. This year a
good rain fell, there was blessing and abundance.

145
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,000
Maşelleh, te evê... te êdî amade kir, te amade kir...
 
Mashallah, you've... you've already prepared it, you
prepared it...

146
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Wile me pir meraq kir, gazî te û wî ra min kir. Em hêsîr in,
xwarina me bixwin na?
 
By God we were very curious, I called you and him. We are
captives, aren't you going to eat our food?

147
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Hingî hûn çûn yan na?
 
Did you go then or not?

148
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
Wileh em neçûn ê. Bes dîk me xwarin.
 
By God we didn't go. We only ate roosters.

149
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:36,000
Te xwar, te xwar, li Fransayê jî te xwar.
 
You ate, you ate, you even ate in France.

150
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:39,000
Li Fransayê me tiştekî bixwe da'wet kir û me xwar.
 
In France we invited ourselves to something and we ate.

151
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:43,000
Oy me go qurban, tiştê ku tu bi destê xwe bikî her xweş e.
 
Oh I said darling, whatever you make with your own hands is
always good.

152
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:45,000
Her xweş e, belê. Ez pir kêfxweş im dayê.
 
It's always good, yes. I am very happy, mother.

153
00:10:45,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Dilbîn, tiştekî ji me ra xeber de, ez nizanim em kê... taruf
bikin jî...
 
Dilbîn, tell us something, I don't know who we should...
introduce...

154
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Min got dayê, tiştî deh-sêzdeh sal e ku hatine milkê xwe. Û
hinekî donikê Badîna jî ji me ra çêkiriye.
 
I said mother, it's been thirteen years since they came to
their property. And she also made us some Badina donik.

155
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:06,000
Ehlen we sehlen. Mil Brîtanyayê jî, miletên serê... şorbe û
donikê Badîna da çêkirin.
 
Welcome. From Britain too, for the guests on the fire... I
made soup and Badina donik.

156
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,000
O, te xwar mamoste te xwar.
 
Oh, you ate teacher, you ate.

157
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Me ezîmet kir, belê.
 
We invited them, yes.

158
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Û xwarin çêkirin. Min go kî jê... şorbe û donik bixwin.
 
And we made food. I said who among them... wants to eat soup
and donik.

159
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Go wile, dila, go, xwarinên we gişt xweş bin, bes go donik û
şorbe go, yanî, ecêb, mam go, axa xweş e.
 
They said, by God, Dila, they said, may all your food be
good, but they said donik and soup, they said, I mean,
amazing, he remained saying, the land is good.

160
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
E, axa wê xweş e.
 
Yes, its land is good.

161
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Xwedê te silamet bike. Ez pir kêfxweş im. Donikê Badîna ka
kî çêdike kek Xelîl?
 
May God keep you safe. I am very happy. Who makes the Badina
donik, brother Xelîl?

162
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:33,000
Pir tiştan dikin, bes... naha meselen kulfetê min ne ji
Badîna ye.
 
They make many things, but... right now for example, my wife
is not from Badina.

163
00:11:33,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Dê kêm be, ji qederê alemê, ez ji terefî... meselen, ez
dibêjim ji min ra donik bika, heta ku ez têm kar, heta
têm...
 
She will fall short, compared to others, from my side... for
example, I say make me donik, until I come from work, until
I come...

164
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:43,000
...ez têm, ez dixwim, dibê xweş e. Ez dibêm xweş e, bes ne
wekî yê dêya min e.
 
...I come, I eat, she says is it good. I say it's good, but
it's not like my mother's.

165
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:48,000
Naha ev... ev vîdîo dê sirke... Silavên me ji dayika zaran
ra jî hene, û ji zarokan ra jî.
 
Now this... this video will keep going... We send our
greetings to the mother of the children, and to the children
as well.

166
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,000
Saet xweş, saet xweş.
 
Good hours, good hours.

167
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Ewan naha carekê dîtin. Naha mekteb e. Vê carê kekê Dilovan
û dayîka xwe hatin.
 
They have only seen it once for now. Right now it's school
time. This time brother Dilovan and his mother came.

168
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Înşelleh bi xwestiyê da em ê werin û herin û, tu zanî Xelîl,
mantiqe... yanî tahmekî din e.
 
God willing, willingly, we will come and go, and, you know
Xelîl, the region... I mean, it has a different taste.

169
00:11:59,000 --> 00:12:00,000
Erê, bi kêfa xweş e.
 
Yes, with pleasure.

170
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:09,000
Yavaş yavaş, meselen meriv dixwaze... meselen meriv hat
gund. Naha meselen, çiyayên li gund in... ew ha, gund e.
Şixul, gund e.
 
Slowly, for example one wants... for example one came to the
village. Right now for example, the mountains in the
village... that is, it's the village. Work, is the village.

171
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Meselen, her yek wê tiştekî bike. Saetên xwe gund derbas
dike, xwarina gund dixwe. Yanî, saetên xwe xweş derbas dike.
 
For example, everyone will do something. Spending their
hours in the village, eating the village food. I mean, they
pass their time nicely.

172
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Qisira ev kar, wextê ez têm gundî xwe. Ez dibînim gundê min
rind e, pak e. Yanî, ez hekî kêftir dibim, zanî?
 
The essence of this work, is when I come to my village. I
see my village is nice, it is clean. I mean, I become much
happier, you know?

173
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:20,000
Belê.
 
Yes.

174
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Û înşelleh em ê yavaş yavaş werin, qeçik jî wê werin bi
dera...
 
And God willing we will come slowly, the children will also
come outside...

175
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Em ê wa jî bi'elîmînin. Ev der, axa kalikên me ye, ev ax
erda me ye, ev dar in...
 
We will teach them too. This place, is the land of our
ancestors, this soil is our earth, these are our trees...

176
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:31,000
Naha tu zanî qeçkên me Sûriyê nedîtine.
 
Now you know our children haven't seen Syria.

177
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Belê, kesên li Ewropayê dibînin, ew bes...
 
Yes, those in Europe see it, they just...

178
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Zarokên we welat nedîtine. Qenatî min, wê werin, wê
bixwazin.
 
Your children haven't seen the country. In my opinion, they
will come, they will want it.

179
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Gava Almanî û Brîtanî tên, em jî wê werin, çima nayên?
 
When Germans and Brits come, we will come too, why wouldn't
they come?

180
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:48,000
Qenatê te bixwazin înşelleh wê bi'elîmin, her tiştekî bi
çavê xwe bibînin, bab û kalên wan çi kirin, wekî dayîk, ez
wan bihesibînim û ez meraq dikim naha.
 
Your belief is that they will want it, God willing they will
learn, see everything with their own eyes, what their
ancestors did, like a mother, I will consider them and I am
curious now.

181
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Erê, belê.
 
Yes, definitely.

182
00:12:49,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Em mezin bûn li vî gundî, her tiştên xweş me tê de dîtin.
 
We grew up in this village, we saw all the beautiful things
in it.

183
00:13:21,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Çiqas sal û emrê me çû, me nizanî çawa derbas bûn.
 
How many years and our life passed, we didn't know how they
went by.

184
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Hêmber çavan rûyên şêrîn, digirîm ji wan wextên şêrîn.
 
Sweet faces before my eyes, I cry from those sweet times.

185
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:38,000
Çi xweş bû zemanê paşîn, çêrokan tiştî bibînim.
 
How beautiful were the past times, to find things in
stories.

186
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:43,000
Şefeqa sibe radibûn, dengê dîkan û reşan dibûn.
 
Waking up at the crack of dawn, the sound of roosters and
darkness fading.

187
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Azana sibe radibûn, her kes bi kar û şixulê xwe bû.
 
Waking up at the morning call to prayer, everyone was at
their job and work.

188
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:53,000
Pîzolên havkûv dibûn, bi kene û xweş rewa dibûn.
 
The elders were gathering, laughing and passing the time
nicely.

189
00:13:53,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Şivanan kar û berx kirin, hawayê wî huşk û beraq bûn.
 
The shepherds were with the sheep and lambs, its weather was
dry and clear.

190
00:13:58,000 --> 00:14:02,000
Rojên gundê min.
 
The days of my village.

191
00:14:02,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Hêmber çavê min.
 
Before my eyes.

192
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Naha, dayîka te, dayîka Dilovan... got ji me ra donikê
Badîna çêkiriye.
 
Now, your mother, Dilovan's mother... said she made us
Badina donik.

193
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Û te wileh. Donikê Badîna çend cureyan çêdikin?
 
By God, yes. How many types of Badina donik do they make?

194
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:15,000
Yek donikê biharê heye...
 
There is one spring donik...

195
00:14:15,000 --> 00:14:19,000
Bi biharê wextên pîvazan, sîr e... ev tiştên hêşîn e.
 
In the spring during the time of onions, it's garlic...
these green things.

196
00:14:19,000 --> 00:14:21,000
Û ne'nê hêşîn.
 
And green mint.

197
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Û em dikin bulxur... tedîqe qawurînin, ê bulxurê hûr.
 
And we make bulgur... slightly fry it, the fine bulgur.

198
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:30,000
Û di nav da hevek pîvaz û vaxtanî da dikin.
 
And inside it they put some onions and greens.

199
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:34,000
Û dimsê bacanan û piçekî dimsê îsotan jî dikinê.
 
And tomato paste and a little pepper paste too.

200
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Li hev dixin û dikin, ew donikê biharê ye.
 
They mix it together and make it, that is the spring donik.

201
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Ewê biharê ye?
 
That's the spring one?

202
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:39,000
Ew ê biharê ye.
 
That is the spring one.

203
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:47,000
Ê zivistanê me va diçêkir, bes me pîvazê hişk û dimsê îsotê,
evana em di zeyta xwe da qawirand û me çêdikirin...
 
The winter one we were just making, but we just dried onions
and pepper paste, we roasted these in our oil and made it...

204
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
Me avê da dikirê, ew jî pir pir xweş dibe.
 
We would put it in the water, and that also becomes very
very good.

205
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:54,000
Belê. Ecêb, ewa ku te çêkir... te qet li Ewropayê jî çêdikir
donikê Badîna?
 
Yes. Amazing, that one you made... did you ever make Badina
donik in Europe too?

206
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Wileh me bi caran çêdikir.
 
By God we made it sometimes.

207
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Me li Swêdê jî çêkiriye, xaltîk li ser êr... Û em çûn
Brîtanyayê jî, me li ser êr çêkir.
 
We made it in Sweden too, aunt on the fire... And we went to
Britain too, we made it on the fire.

208
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Ê da, vê carê jî... em li nav milkê xwe, li milkê xwedî...
bes xalî em dest nedanê.
 
Yes, and this time too... we are in our property, in the
property of the owner... but we empty, didn't touch it.

209
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Xwedê jê qayîl be, kekê me da ye...
 
May God be pleased with him, our brother gave it...

210
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:22,000
Saet xweş. Kaka Dilovan, dîsa bêm... tiştekî xwes li
Brîtanya çi ye? Te dît, tu dixwazî yanî çi seqafe û çi tişt
heye ku te dît, xwest em bînin welatê Efrînê?
 
Good hours. Brother Dilovan, I'll come back... what is a
beautiful thing in Britain? You saw, you want, I mean what
culture and what things are there that you saw, you wished
we could bring to the country of Efrîn?

211
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:30,000
Naha... tiştê ku ez silav dikim meselen wa ye... ajotina
makîneyan... Meriv dixwaze tiştê ku xelk ajotina wan bibîne.
 
Now... the thing I greet for example is that... driving
cars... A person wants the thing that people see their
driving.

212
00:15:30,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Nabe me'ne meriv bide xestiyê çimkî şixulê xelkê ecele ye,
ne.
 
It doesn't mean one should hit the accelerator because
people's work is rushed, no.

213
00:15:35,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Yanî wê me'neyê çimkî fawda çêdibe.
 
I mean in that sense because chaos happens.

214
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:44,000
Û yanî tişkî wê evda hebî... ê, sere ajotinê pir rind e
meselen a xweş dibe...
 
And I mean there should be a thing of peace... uh, the start
of driving is very good for example it becomes nice...

215
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Meriv dixe xwesta wê wek... qeçk... cuçik... pîremer...
keçikî dî makîne... or tê xistî... fîgoriya pey dev xwe,
xort dimîne, se... zembela wî kuçkî çi ye? Nizanim...
 
One drives on the request as if... children... chicks... old
man... another girl a car... comes and hits... he turns his
head around, a young man stays, wait... what is the basket
of that dog? I don't know...

216
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Yanî bi Brîtanyayê jî hene, ev xwedê çêdibin, wile tarîbên
wê naçêdibin çêdibin.
 
